{"diagnosis": "Loopback data got 0xff (idle) want 0xa5, ser_tx/send_pattern never held correct start/data timing. send_divcnt threshold uses (cfg_divider >> 4) on line 130, making TX bit period ~5 cycles instead of divider 64, 16x too fast for the configured baud. Loopback RX therefore samples idle and reports 0xff.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b0};
 				send_bitcnt <= 10;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
-			if (send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) && send_bitcnt) begin
+			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;", "expected": "tohost PASS (was FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP uart data mismatch, loopback got 0xa5 as expected"}

